@meta
id: 12-14
title: Land on the end of the match
chapter: 12
type: lesson
skills: search-offset
par: 48
minutes: 5
vscode: find it, click just after it, type
open: payout.provider.ts

@brief
Payout amounts are being sent to the ledger in pounds while the ledger
counts in pence. In `quote`, the line

    const amount = order.total;

needs to become

    const amount = order.total * 100;

A search normally drops you on the *first* character of what you matched,
which is the wrong end when the thing you want to do is add something
after it. You can shuffle along with `e` or `$` afterwards, and on a
one-word match that is fine — but `order.total` is not one word, and `$`
would put you after the semicolon.

A search can be told where to land.

@keys
| `/text/e` `Enter` | search, but put the cursor on the last character of the match |
| `/text/b` `Enter` | on the first character — the default, spelled out |
| `/text/e+1` `Enter` | one character past the end of the match |
| `a` | append after the cursor |

@hints
The search itself is easy; the problem is where it leaves you. A search
can carry an instruction about where to put the cursor.
--
Adding `/e` to the end of a pattern means "end of the match". So
`/something/e` `Enter` lands on the last character of `something` rather
than the first.
--
`/const amount = order.total/e` `Enter` leaves the cursor on the final
`l`. From there `a` and the text you are adding.

@solution
/const amount = order.total/e<Enter>  a * 100<Esc>  :wq<Enter>

An offset is the bit after the second slash. `/e` is the one you will use
most: it means "having found the match, sit on its last character". `/b`
means the beginning, which is the default and is worth knowing only so
that `/b+2` and friends make sense — offsets take a number, so `/e+1` is
one past the end and `/b+3` is three characters into the match.

Why bother, when `e` or `w` would move you along afterwards? Two reasons.
The first is that a match is not a word: `order.total` is three words to
vim, and `https://payouts.internal` is a small crowd of them. Counting
word motions to get to the end of a match is fiddly and breaks when the
match changes. The offset always means the same thing.

The second reason is the one that makes offsets worth a chapter slot at
all, and it is the next lesson: an offset changes what an operator does,
not just where the cursor stops.

@start payout.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from '../order/order.repository';
import { PayoutRepository } from './payout.repository';
import { LedgerService } from '../../infrastructure/services/ledger.service';

@injectable()
export class PayoutProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PayoutRepository) protected payoutRepository: PayoutRepository,
    @inject(LedgerService) protected ledgerService: LedgerService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(args: { id: string }) {
    const payout = await this.payoutRepository.findOne({ where: { id: args.id } });

    if (!payout) {
      throw exception('PAYOUT_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return payout;
  }

  public async quote(args: { orderId: string }) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id: args.orderId } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    const amount = order.total;
    const fee = Math.round(amount * 0.029) + 25;

    return { orderId: order.id, amount, fee, net: amount - fee };
  }

  public async schedule(args: { orderId: string; amount: number }) {
    const payout = await this.payoutRepository.create({
      values: { orderId: args.orderId, amount: args.amount, status: 'SCHEDULED' },
    });

    await this.ledgerService.record({
      reference: payout.id,
      amount: args.amount,
      direction: 'CREDIT',
    });

    return payout;
  }

  public async cancel(args: { id: string }) {
    const payout = await this.findOne({ id: args.id });

    if (payout.status !== 'SCHEDULED') {
      throw exception('PAYOUT_ALREADY_SENT');
    }

    return this.payoutRepository.update({
      where: { id: payout.id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected payout.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from '../order/order.repository';
import { PayoutRepository } from './payout.repository';
import { LedgerService } from '../../infrastructure/services/ledger.service';

@injectable()
export class PayoutProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PayoutRepository) protected payoutRepository: PayoutRepository,
    @inject(LedgerService) protected ledgerService: LedgerService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(args: { id: string }) {
    const payout = await this.payoutRepository.findOne({ where: { id: args.id } });

    if (!payout) {
      throw exception('PAYOUT_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return payout;
  }

  public async quote(args: { orderId: string }) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id: args.orderId } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    const amount = order.total * 100;
    const fee = Math.round(amount * 0.029) + 25;

    return { orderId: order.id, amount, fee, net: amount - fee };
  }

  public async schedule(args: { orderId: string; amount: number }) {
    const payout = await this.payoutRepository.create({
      values: { orderId: args.orderId, amount: args.amount, status: 'SCHEDULED' },
    });

    await this.ledgerService.record({
      reference: payout.id,
      amount: args.amount,
      direction: 'CREDIT',
    });

    return payout;
  }

  public async cancel(args: { id: string }) {
    const payout = await this.findOne({ id: args.id });

    if (payout.status !== 'SCHEDULED') {
      throw exception('PAYOUT_ALREADY_SENT');
    }

    return this.payoutRepository.update({
      where: { id: payout.id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}
